.context BLBX
This model passes the feed through to the tailing. A water stream can be connected directly to the unit. This model can be changed using the software development kit to suit your needs.
.context CBOX
This is a simple splitter model. The model is written in C and the source code is accessible in Developer Studio. It can be used as a template for new models written in C.
Parameters:
  Fractional split to tailing

.context NAGE
This model was developed at the Julius Kruttschnitt Mineral Research Centre and is an extension of the original model for the performance of the hydrocyclone that was developed by Lynch and Rao. This model was developed by multilinear regression of experimental data that was obtained from tests on several Krebs cyclones. The model consists of empirical relationships for predicting D50c, the flow through the hydrocyclone as a function of the pressure drop and the fractional recovery of the water. The exponential sum model is used for the partition function. 

The model, as presented by the authors, also includes an empirical expression for the prediction of the fractional recovery by volume of total feed to the underflow.  However this makes the model internally inconsistent because the volumetric recovery of solids is determine completely by the calculated D50c, the assumed classification function and the water recovery. The total volumetric recovery is defined as a combination of the volumetric recovery of the solids and the volumetrivc recovery of the water and this is always inconsistent with the separate model prediction of the total volumetric recovery. Consequently the model for the total volumetric recovery is not used for the simulation of performance of the unit but it is used to compare with the calculated value and to return the extent of the inconsistency in the report file for the unit.

Parameters:
  Calibration factor for D50c   KD0
  Calibration factor for total slurry flowrate    KQ0
  Calibration factor for water recovery to underflow    KW1
  Efficiency factor for the classification function.
  Diameter of cyclindrical section
  Inlet diameter (diameter of circle of same area as cyclone inlet)
  Overflow (vortex finder) diameter
  Underflow (apex) diameter
  Length of cylindrical section
  Cone full angle (degrees)




